Say when a kext's start() returns

The boot stops right after AppleARMPPlatform's interrupt controller prints 'not
registrying member at registerService()'.  That print comes from the driver's own
start routine, which the kernel cannot instrument, but its return does pass
through OSKext::start().

Print the return code and the identifier at the function's single exit, so a
photo tells whether the driver's start came back or is still inside it.
---
diff --git a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
index d14d5c1..8f3e9e6 100644
--- a/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
+++ b/libkern/c++/OSKext.cpp
@@ -8312,6 +8312,15 @@ OSKext::start(bool startDependenciesFlag)
 	}
 
 finish:
+	/*
+	 * nio: every start() leaves through here.  The boot stops right after
+	 * AppleARMPPlatform's interrupt controller prints its registerService
+	 * line, and that print comes from the driver's own start routine, which
+	 * the kernel cannot instrument -- but its return passes through this
+	 * function.  This line says whether start() came back or is still inside.
+	 */
+	printf("nio: kext start ret=0x%x id=[%s]\n", (unsigned int)result,
+	    (getIdentifierCString() != NULL) ? getIdentifierCString() : "(null)");
 	return result;
 }
 
